  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Pennsylvania has received $19B in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. The state has 378,777 awards with an average award size of $50.1K, and obligations fell 29.6% year over year. The Department of Defense is the largest buyer, obligating $15.1B in the current fiscal year to date. Major vendors include AMERISOURCEBERGEN DRUG CORP with $4.7B and FLUOR MARINE PROPULSION, LLC with $4B. Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences (except Nanotechnology and Biotechnology) is the largest industry by obligations at $4.5B, followed by Medicinal and Botanical Manufacturing at $3.2B and Power Boiler and Heat Exchanger Manufacturing at $2.1B. Historical fiscal-year totals show obligations rose from $17.6B in FY21 to $26.9B in FY25 before the current-year total of $19B. These figures reflect contract obligations only and represent fiscal year to date totals when the period is partial.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How does FY2026 spending compare to prior fiscal years?",
        "body": "FY2026 obligations stand at $19B compared with $26.9B in FY25 and $26.6B in FY24. FY23 obligations were $23.3B, FY22 obligations were $19.7B, and FY21 obligations were $17.6B. Obligations fell 29.6% year over year."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies, vendors, and industries dominate Pennsylvania federal contracting?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense leads buying with $15.1B in obligations for FY2026 to date, followed by the Department of Energy with $2B. Top vendors include AMERISOURCEBERGEN DRUG CORP at $4.7B and FLUOR MARINE PROPULSION, LLC at $4B. Leading industries by obligations are Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences (except Nanotechnology and Biotechnology) at $4.5B and Medicinal and Botanical Manufacturing at $3.2B."
      }
    ]
  },
